1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:19,360
I'm Jessi, and this is my suitcase.

2
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:25,120
But before I show you what I've got inside, I'm going to make a very public confession,

3
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:28,960
and that is I'm outfit obsessed.

4
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:36,080
I love finding, wearing, and more recently, photographing and blogging a different, colorful,

5
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,560
crazy outfit for every single occasion.

6
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:42,280
But I don't buy anything new.

7
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:46,720
I get all my clothes secondhand from flea markets and thrift stores.

8
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:50,800
Oh, thank you!

9
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:55,920
Secondhand shopping allows me to reduce the impact my wardrobe has on the environment

10
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,400
and on my wallet.

11
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,320
I get to meet all kinds of great people.

12
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,600
My dollars usually go to a good cause.

13
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:07,880
I look pretty unique, and it makes shopping like my own personal treasure hunt.

14
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:10,080
I mean, what am I going to find today?

15
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,480
Is it going to be my size?

16
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,520
Will I like the color?

17
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,680
Will it be under $20?

18
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:20,720
If all the answers are yes, I feel as though I've won.

19
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:27,080
I want to get back to my suitcase and tell you what I packed for this exciting week here

20
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,080
at TED.

21
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:30,880
I mean, what does somebody with all these outfits bring with her?

22
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:34,440
So I'm going to show you exactly what I brought.

23
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:41,600
I brought seven pairs of underpants, and that's it.

24
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:46,240
Exactly one week's worth of undies is all I put in my suitcase.

25
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:51,620
I was betting that I'd be able to find everything else I could possibly want to wear once I

26
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:53,820
got here to Palm Springs.

27
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:59,740
And since you don't know me as the woman walking around TED in her underwear, that

28
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:04,340
means I found a few things, and I'd really love to show you my week's worth of outfits

29
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:05,340
right now.

30
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:06,340
Does that sound good?

31
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:14,540
So as I do this, I'm also going to tell you a few of the life lessons that, believe it

32
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:18,600
or not, I have picked up in these adventures wearing nothing new.

33
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,260
So let's start with Sunday.

34
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:23,220
I call this shiny tiger.

35
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:26,540
You do not have to spend a lot of money to look great.

36
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:30,560
You can almost always look phenomenal for under $50.

37
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:35,900
This whole outfit, including the jacket, cost me $55, and it was the most expensive thing

38
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:38,460
that I wore the entire week.

39
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:41,220
Monday, color is powerful.

40
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:46,520
It is almost physiologically impossible to be in a bad mood when you're wearing bright

41
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:48,020
red pants.

42
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:55,020
If you are happy, you are going to attract other happy people to you.

43
00:02:55,020 --> 00:03:00,300
Tuesday, fitting in is way overrated.

44
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:05,540
I spent a whole lot of my life trying to be myself and at the same time fit in.

45
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:07,620
Just be who you are.

46
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:12,820
If you are surrounding yourself with the right people, they will not only get it, they will

47
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,940
appreciate it.

48
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,860
Wednesday, embrace your inner child.

49
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:24,340
Sometimes people tell me that I look like I'm playing dress up or that I remind them

50
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,700
of their seven-year-old.

51
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:31,420
I like to smile and say thank you.

52
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:34,760
Thursday, confidence is key.

53
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:39,160
If you think you look good in something, you almost certainly do.

54
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:43,340
And if you don't think you look good in something, you're also probably right.

55
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,620
I grew up with a mom who taught me this day in and day out.

56
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:50,740
But it wasn't until I turned 30 that I really got what this meant.

57
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:54,180
And I'm going to break it down for you for just a second.

58
00:03:54,180 --> 00:04:00,980
If you believe you're a beautiful person, inside and out, there is no look that you

59
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:02,420
can't pull off.

60
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:05,060
So there is no excuse for any of us here in this audience.

61
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:07,740
We should be able to rock anything we want to rock.

62
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:09,580
Thank you.

63
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:20,940
Friday, a universal truth, five words for you, gold sequins go with everything.

64
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:27,260
And finally, Saturday, developing your own unique personal style is a really great way

65
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:31,220
to tell the world something about you without having to say a word.

66
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:35,060
It's been proven to me time and time again as people have walked up to me this week simply

67
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,940
because of what I'm wearing.

68
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:39,120
And we've had great conversations.

69
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:43,180
So obviously this is not all going to fit back in my tiny suitcase.

70
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:47,920
So before I go home to Brooklyn, I'm going to donate everything back because the lesson

71
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:52,440
I'm trying to learn myself this week is that it's okay to let go.

72
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:57,440
I don't need to get emotionally attached to these things because around the corner, there's

73
00:04:57,440 --> 00:05:04,880
always going to be another crazy, colorful, shiny outfit just waiting for me if I put

74
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:07,880
a little love in my heart and look.

75
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:08,880
Thank you very much.

76
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:08,900
Thank you.

